WEBVTT

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.616
Because she'd be like, you know --
she'd get on the phone.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.336
She'd be like, "Harry,
it's better than the drugs.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.324
She was fantastic.

00:03:08.348 --> 00:03:11.576
So I found myself getting this stuff,
thanks to her assist,

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.856
and suddenly, you know,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.976
I had a synthesizer
when I was 14 years old --

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.216
this kind of stuff.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.296
And it let me make things,
which, to me, was sort of the dream.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.856
He sort of humored my obsession
to other things too, like magic.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.616
The thing is, we'd go
to this magic store in New York City

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.016
called Lou Tannen's Magic.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.496
It was this great magic store.